  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Philippines  - Cyclone Tropical Storm Kristine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">97,250 people</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention includes:

Distribution of essential household and shelter items.
Cash assistance for basic needs and livelihoods recovery.
Deployment of health and WASH (water, sanitation, and hygiene) services.
Provision of psychosocial support and child-friendly spaces.
Reconstruction of schools and communal facilities.
Community engagement for inclusive and accountable response.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention spans 16 provinces across the Philippines, including areas in:

Region 2: Aurora, Cagayan, Isabela, Quirino, and Nueva Vizcaya.
CAR: Apayao.
Region 5 (Bicol): Camarines Sur, Camarines Norte, Albay, Catanduanes, Sorsogon, and Masbate.
Region 4A (Calabarzon): Batangas, Laguna, Cavite, and Quezon.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation addresses the impact of a series of tropical cyclones and floods in the Philippines, aiming to support 97,250 affected people (19,450 families). It focuses on providing emergency relief, early recovery assistance, and resilience-building in the affected communities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation is necessary due to the unprecedented occurrence of six consecutive tropical cyclones (including Typhoons Kristine, Leon, Marce, Nika, Ofel, and Pepito) that caused widespread damage. Over 10 million people were affected, with significant damage to homes, livelihoods, infrastructure, and education, leaving communities vulnerable and in urgent need of assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
